{
  "summary": "A reporter enters the DVDASA room and becomes part of the episode. The result is both a revealing press-power document and a difficult consent record: David explains his distrust of edited profiles, tests Jay Caspian Kang's identity and clothes, describes adult friendship and sudden fame, assigns Critter an expanding set of informal jobs, and narrates celebrity and art-party encounters. Around those threads, the cast spends nearly half an hour escalating assault hypotheticals, pressures Bobby past repeated refusals, speculates about childhood abuse without evidence, exposes private relationship material, gives unsafe wart advice, and threatens the observing reporter. The archive should make all of that legible without laundering threats into charm or turning uncertain memories into accusations.",
